173
00:06:50,639 --> 00:06:55,919
rectangular shape in frequency.

174
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:58,319
Next, when we write out the convolution,

175
00:06:55,919 --> 00:07:01,120
we see it as an infinite sum, a series

176
00:06:58,319 --> 00:07:03,199
of shifted sync functions. Each one is

177
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:05,360
scaled by the value of our signal at a

178
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:07,759
sample point. The distance between these

179
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:09,919
samples is delta t, and that's simply 1

180
00:07:07,759 --> 00:07:11,759
over p, the spacing in the frequency

181
00:07:09,919 --> 00:07:13,680
domain.

182
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:16,080
The final line is the famous Shannon

183
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:18,160
interpolation formula. In words, it

184
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:20,160
says, "Take each sample of your signal,

185
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:22,639
put a sync function centered at that

186
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:24,960
sample, scale it by the sample's value,

187
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:27,039
and then add them all together. Do this

188
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:29,360
for every sample, stretching infinitely

189
00:07:27,039 --> 00:07:32,160
in both directions, and you get your

190
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:34,000
original continuous signal back exactly

191
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:35,919
as long as the sampling conditions are

192
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,560
satisfied.

193
00:07:35,919 --> 00:07:40,639
This is a beautiful result. It tells us

194
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:42,720
that perfect reconstruction is not just

195
00:07:40,639 --> 00:07:45,039
possible. It's a direct consequence of

196
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:46,800
the sampling theorem. And this formula

197
00:07:45,039 --> 00:07:50,759
is one of the core foundations of all

198
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,759
digital signal processing.

199
00:07:52,479 --> 00:07:56,319
Let's look at a good case when our

200
00:07:54,479 --> 00:07:59,280
sampling rate is high enough to meet the

201
00:07:56,319 --> 00:08:01,120
sampling theorem's requirement.

202
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:03,440
The black curve here is our original

203
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:05,919
continuous signal. Think of it as the

204
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:08,319
true signal. The blue points show where

205
00:08:05,919 --> 00:08:11,599
we took our samples. A limited number of

206
00:08:08,319 --> 00:08:13,759
values spaced evenly in time.

207
00:08:11,599 --> 00:08:15,599
Here's the magic. If the sampling rate

208
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:17,599
