776
00:30:43,279 --> 00:30:49,679
A few quick anchors. TN= to N / P are

777
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:53,279
the time samples. U M equals to M / T

778
00:30:49,679 --> 00:30:56,880
are the frequency samples.

779
00:30:53,279 --> 00:31:00,880
The exponential E the minus J2 pi MN /N

780
00:30:56,880 --> 00:31:03,120
is the rotating basis wave.

781
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:05,360
Next, we'll write the inverse D of T and

782
00:31:03,120 --> 00:31:07,520
see why a factor of 1 /N naturally

783
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:11,080
appears. So we can reconstruct the time

784
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:11,080
samples exactly.

785
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:17,679
Up to now, we've been writing our time

786
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:20,880
samples as T0, T1, T2, and so on. and

787
00:31:17,679 --> 00:31:23,039
our frequency samples as U0, U1, U2 and

788
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:24,559
so on. But when we work with sample

789
00:31:23,039 --> 00:31:28,799
data, what really matters are the

790
00:31:24,559 --> 00:31:30,960
integer positions of these samples.

791
00:31:28,799 --> 00:31:33,760
So to make things simpler, we'll label

792
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:36,480
them using integers in square brackets.

793
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:39,919
For example, f of0 means the value of

794
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:42,000
the function at time sample t0.

795
00:31:39,919 --> 00:31:43,760
Of one means the value at time sample

796
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:45,840
t1.

797
00:31:43,760 --> 00:31:49,120
f of n minus one means the value at the

798
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:51,360
last time sample tn minus one.

799
00:31:49,120 --> 00:31:54,240
We do the same in the frequency domain.

800
00:31:51,360 --> 00:31:57,120
fhat of 0 means the fora transform value

801
00:31:54,240 --> 00:32:00,399
at frequency sample u0.

802
00:31:57,120 --> 00:32:03,519
fhat of 1 is at u1 and so on up to fhat

803
00:32:00,399 --> 00:32:05,840
of n minus one.

804
00:32:03,519 --> 00:32:08,640
With this notation, the discrete fier

805
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:11,600
transform reads like this. fhat of m

806
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:14,399
equals the sum from n= 0 to n minus 1 of

807
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:18,799
f of n multiplied by e ^ of minus j

808
00:32:14,399 --> 00:32:20,880
2<unk> m * n / n.

809
00:32:18,799 --> 00:32:23,039
Here n is the index for time domain

810
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:24,960
samples and m is the index for frequency

811
00:32:23,039 --> 00:32:27,279
components.

812
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:29,519
Each term is just the sample value f of

813
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:32,159
n multiplied by a sinosoidal basis wave

814
00:32:29,519 --> 00:32:33,840
at frequency index m. Adding all those

815
00:32:32,159 --> 00:32:36,080
